      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An investigation into the structure-activity relationship of a lead compound, prolyl-5-aminopentanoic acid 4, led to the identification of a novel series of 4-piperidinylacetic acid, 1-piperazinylacetic acid, and 4-aminobenzoic acid derivatives as potent VLA-4 antagonists with low nanomolar IC(50) values. A representative compound morpholinyl-4-piperidinylacetic acid derivative (13d: IC(50)=4.4 nM) showed efficacy in the Ascaris-antigen sensitized murine airway inflammation model by oral administration."},
